.TH RIPNET 1 "September 2026" "ripnet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ripnet \- network diagnostics, packet analysis, and authorized testing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ripnet
.I command
.RI [ target ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ripnet --help
.br
.B ripnet --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ripnet
is a command-line toolkit for network diagnostics, packet analysis, observability, discovery, and authorized load testing. Commands are grouped by workflow and can emit human-readable output or JSON where supported.
.PP
Use
.B ripnet COMMAND --help
to review the available options. Some operations require elevated privileges, libpcap support, or platform-specific adapters.
.SH COMMAND FAMILIES
.TP
.B Interfaces and capture
.BR list-interfaces , show-stats , capture
.TP
.B Reachability and routes
.BR ping , ping-tcp , ping-udp , ping-sweep , traceroute , traceroute-tcp , traceroute-udp , traceroute-icmp
.TP
.B Scanning
.BR scan , port-scan , network-scan , service-scan , os-fingerprint , udp-scan , syn-scan , fin-scan , xmas-scan , null-scan
.TP
.B DNS
.BR dns-lookup , dns-reverse , dns-query , dns-server-test , dns-trace , dns-bruteforce , dns-zone-transfer , dnssec-verify , dns-cache-flush
.TP
.B Local discovery
.BR arp-table , arp-scan , arp-request , arp-reply , arp-cache-add , arp-cache-delete , arp-spoof-detect , discovery-ping , discovery-arp , discovery-dns , discovery-mdns , discovery-llmnr , discovery-netbios , discovery-smb , discovery-http , discovery-ssl , discovery-snmp , discovery-upnp
.TP
.B System visibility
.BR netstat , netstat-listening , netstat-route , netstat-process , netstat-interface , netstat-group , netstat-timer , scan-processes , route-table , route-get , route-trace , route-monitor
.TP
.B Firewall and monitoring
.BR firewall-status , firewall-log , firewall-add , firewall-delete , firewall-flush , block-ip , unblock-ip , block-port , unblock-port , bandwidth-test , bandwidth-monitor , monitor-start , monitor-stop , monitor-status , monitor-alert , monitor-log , monitor-export
.TP
.B Security and authorized stress testing
.BR ssh , security-ssh , sftp , security-http , security-ssl , security-smtp , security-banner , security-dns , security-audit , security-scan , tcp-stress , http-stress , packet-flood , ping-flood , port-knocking
.TP
.B HTTP
.BR http-request , http-bulk
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , --help
Show the command and flag reference.
.TP
.BR -v , --version
Print the installed ripnet version.
.TP
.BR -i\ NAME , --interface\ NAME
Select a network interface.
.TP
.BR -H\ HOST , --host\ HOST
Set the target host.
.TP
.BR -n\ CIDR , --network\ CIDR
Set the target network.
.PP
.B network-scan
accepts IPv4 CIDR targets containing at most 4096 addresses. Network and
broadcast addresses are excluded for prefixes through /30; /31 and /32
addresses are included. Without --port, the command only enumerates target
addresses are included. The command requires --port and attempts TCP
connections; an unsuccessful connection does not prove that a host is offline.
.B ping-sweep
uses ICMP echo and reports only hosts that respond. Missing responses are not
proof that a host is offline.
.TP
.BR -p\ N , --port\ N
Set a target port.
.TP
.BR -sp\ N , --start-port\ N
Set the first port for a range. The default is 1.
.TP
.BR -ep\ N , --end-port\ N
Set the last port for a range. The default is 1024.
.TP
.BR -t\ MS , --timeout\ MS
Set the operation timeout in milliseconds. The default is 1000.
.TP
.BR -c\ N , --count\ N
Set the probe count. The default is 4.
.TP
.BR -r\ TYPE , --record-type\ TYPE
Set the DNS record type. The default is A.
.TP
.BR -s\ HOST , --dns-server\ HOST
Select a DNS server.
.TP
.BR -w\ FILE , --wordlist\ FILE
Select a DNS brute-force wordlist.
.TP
.BR -P\ NAME , --protocol\ NAME
Select a transport protocol.
.TP
.BR -u\ NAME , --user\ NAME
Set the remote SSH or SFTP user.
.TP
.BI --identity\ FILE
Use a private key file.
.TP
.BR -J\ HOST , --jump-host\ HOST
Connect through a jump host.
.TP
.BI --local-forward\ SPEC
Create a local TCP forwarding rule, equivalent to OpenSSH -L.
.TP
.BI --remote-forward\ SPEC
Create a remote TCP forwarding rule, equivalent to OpenSSH -R.
.TP
.BI --dynamic-forward\ SPEC
Create a SOCKS proxy, equivalent to OpenSSH -D.
.TP
.BI --proxy-command\ CMD
Use a custom OpenSSH ProxyCommand.
.TP
.BI --ssh-option\ OPTION
Pass an OpenSSH -o option. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR -A , --agent-forwarding
Forward the SSH agent.
.TP
.BR -X , --x11-forwarding
Enable X11 forwarding.
.TP
.BR -T , --no-tty
Disable pseudo-terminal allocation.
.TP
.BI --remote-path\ PATH
Open an SFTP session at a remote path.
.TP
.BR -j , --json
Emit machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.BR -V , --verbose
Print additional diagnostic details.
.TP
.B -promisc, --promisc
Request promiscuous packet capture.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ripnet list-interfaces
ripnet ping example.com --count 5
ripnet http-request https://example.test/ --json
ripnet http-bulk https://example.test/health --allow-host example.test --count 5 --max-rps 2
ripnet scan 192.0.2.10 --start-port 1 --end-port 1024
ripnet dns-query example.com --record-type MX
ripnet service-scan 192.0.2.10 --port 22
ripnet ping example.com --help
ripnet ssh git@github.com --identity ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
ripnet ssh admin@example.com -L 8080:localhost:80
ripnet sftp deploy@example.com /var/www --identity ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.fi
.SH IMPLEMENTATION LIMITS
.B http-request
uses libcurl for HTTP/1.1 and negotiated HTTP/2 over TLS. TLS verification is
enabled unless --insecure is explicitly supplied. Responses are limited to 16
MiB per request and timeouts default to 1 second. JSON and URL-encoded form
bodies are supported. The bulk command has hard limits of 1000 requests, 8
concurrent workers, 10 requests per second, 16 MiB aggregate request and
response bodies, and 120 seconds of scheduled duration. It requires --allow-host to exactly
match the URL host and does not follow redirects. Continuous-duration and ramp
testing, persistent connection reuse, and request-definition files are not
implemented. The legacy http-stress command is unavailable.
.PP
.B monitor-start
and
.B monitor-stop
are not implemented. The monitor status command performs a one-shot
measurement. The
.B dns-cache-flush
clears ripnet's in-process DNS lookup cache on every platform. On macOS it also flushes
the system resolver by running dscacheutil -flushcache and signaling
mDNSResponder; this requires root, so run it as
.B sudo ripnet dns-cache-flush.
On other platforms it does not clear the system resolver cache. Successful
dns-lookup results are cached in-process for up to 60 seconds, with a maximum
of 4096 entries; failed lookups are not cached. The
.B ddos
command is intentionally unsupported; packet-flood and ping-flood operations
are also unavailable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully, or help or version information was requested.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid or required an argument was missing.
.TP
.B 1
The requested operation failed or is unavailable on the selected platform.
